license: MIT
repository-code: "TODO_REPO_URL"
abstract: >-
  Multimedia representation with 2D Gaussian Splatting. Video is represented as
  a fixed population of 2D Gaussians whose attributes vary over time through
  Chebyshev polynomials, rendered with a differentiable CUDA rasterizer. Audio
  is represented as a sum of Gabor atoms.
keywords:
  - Gaussian Splatting
  - video representation
  - temporal representation
  - temporal interpolation
  - Chebyshev polynomials
  - Gabor atoms
  - multimedia signals
preferred-citation:
